  "verbalization": "Tamulamide B is shown to interact with Carboxylesterase 2 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging through the target molecule (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol. This compound is identified as a target of both MIP and VMRC-LCP, which in turn are targets of Tamulamide B. The presence of this compound as a target of Carboxylesterase 2 suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of this enzyme, which is consistent with the observed scores in the evidence. The indirect pathways through MIP and VMRC-LCP do not provide a direct link to Carboxylesterase 2, but they support a broader network of interactions that may contribute to the overall effect of Tamulamide B. The evidence suggests that Tamulamide B may act by targeting a metabolizing enzyme, possibly through a complex involving multiple molecular targets, which could influence the pharmacological profile of the compound. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering multiple targets in understanding the mechanism of action of Tamulamide B.",
